ed  in order to embed the Charter across all  of their work and secondly and finally  in terms of new tools today we will  launch a new instrument called the  European fundamental rights information  system so-called Efes FRS is an online  resource which for the first time ever  globally will bring together all of the  findings of all of the international  monitoring bodies in the  Human Rights filled country-by-country  right by right and the efforts is  organized according to the chapters and  the categories of the Charter secondly  and finally in terms of how we will  support you we will continue to ensure  that the Charter informs everything that  we do the Charter is our grund norm it  is the legal base on which from which we  start all of our research and our  technical assistance activities it is  also increasingly the heart of our  programs of cooperation with civil  society with National Human Rights  institutions with governments indeed and  with equality bodies and so dear friends  thank you very much for your attention  this morning let me go back in absolute  conclusion to the to the display box at  the Parliament it's not there anymore  it was taken away at some point last  year it was taken away so that the  document itself could be restored that's  find in that also an image for today  today is an opportunity for all of us to  restore ourselves to restore our passion  for our commitment to the Charter of  Fundamental Rights to ensure that it  becomes what its drafters dreamt of the  beating heart of our European project  thank you
 

